APPLY-ROUND-109.cmd SHIPPED TRUNCATED AND COULD NOT HAVE APPLIED THE ROUND.

Found while modelling round 110's script on it. /mnt/user-data/outputs/APPLY-ROUND-109.cmd is 163 lines and ends mid-structure:

  - it announces seven steps and defines FIVE. There is no [6/7] ancestor check and no [7/7] fast-forward;
  - the `if /i "%CURRENT%"=="%TARGET%" (` block opened at its line 127 is NEVER CLOSED -- no matching `)` exists after it;
  - `goto :done` is present at line 128 and the `:done` LABEL IS ABSENT;
  - crucially, `git merge --ff-only refs/remotes/bundle/round109` -- the line that actually moves the branch -- is missing. The script fetches the bundle into refs/remotes/bundle/round109 and then prints a success banner without ever advancing HEAD.

So even had cmd.exe accepted the unbalanced block, the script would have reported 'Applied. HEAD is now 4a13f45' while HEAD stayed where it was. APPLY-ROUND-108.cmd has all of it (lines 171, 173, 186-187, 192), so this is a truncation of a previously correct script rather than a design that was never right.

NO HARM REACHED THE COMMANDER, and that is observed rather than assumed: `git fetch origin` moved origin/codex/pl-ai-0001-repair from 4f23c1d to 4a13f45, so round 109's target is on GitHub and Diego's repository evidently reached it another way.

WHAT THIS CHANGES. A delivery script that prints success without doing the work is the same class of defect as a gate that passes without running -- which is the thing this project refuses six ways in CLAUDE.md -- and it was in the one artefact nothing in this repository checks. Round 110's script is written against APPLY-ROUND-108.cmd's complete structure and is checked MECHANICALLY before delivery: balanced parentheses, every announced step present, every goto's label present, and the fast-forward line present. The checker is reported with the delivery rather than trusted.
